        "pl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "bc0c802d-9fd7-3fc1-be25-40c3bf1968b5",
                "word": "ponadto",
                "pos": "particle",
                "lang_code": "pl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "21726323-26f2-35bd-aee1-7f1a44024f19",
                        "entry_id": "bc0c802d-9fd7-3fc1-be25-40c3bf1968b5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "nawiązuje do poprzedniego kontekstu wypowiedzi i wprowadza nową informację na omawiany już temat"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "31e4340d-17c8-4688-b521-fc07b0d5329d",
                                "sense_id": "21726323-26f2-35bd-aee1-7f1a44024f19",
                                "text": "Pan Adam jest sumienny i pracowity, a ponadto ma długi staż pracy."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a75ddab8-ef5a-4096-b245-16db8dc43ce0",
                        "source_entry_id": "bc0c802d-9fd7-3fc1-be25-40c3bf1968b5",
                        "source_sense_id": "21726323-26f2-35bd-aee1-7f1a44024f19",
                        "target_lang_word": "moreover",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "moreover",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2eb51a57-6120-3755-a51d-d8f0e8006770",
                                        "entry_id": "0fadcc48-33c7-3eb3-a679-59f9fd9f670b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In addition to what has been said."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "conjunctive",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bf60605-eb25-4086-8656-ca0d58fe3a4d",
                                                "sense_id": "2eb51a57-6120-3755-a51d-d8f0e8006770",
                                                "text": "For three years there had been pestilence, and in the last of the three a famine; moreover, there was imminence of war."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd310486-2804-42a7-8e6a-ae2c21ca9509",
                                                "sense_id": "2eb51a57-6120-3755-a51d-d8f0e8006770",
                                                "text": "The characteristics ‘terrestrial’ and ‘two-footed’ are predicated of the species ‘man’, but not present in it. For they are not in man. Moreover, the definition of the differentia may be predicated of that of which the differentia itself is predicated."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c722cabe-44a8-406f-8897-ae70e3d11d73",
                                                "sense_id": "2eb51a57-6120-3755-a51d-d8f0e8006770",
                                                "text": "A curious thing about the ontological problem is its simplicity. It can be put in three Anglo-Saxon monosyllables: ‘What is there?’ It can be answered, moreover, in a word—‘Everything’—and everyone will accept this answer as true."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e844b790-e88e-45dc-ad81-7ced1932b5e4",
                        "source_entry_id": "bc0c802d-9fd7-3fc1-be25-40c3bf1968b5",
                        "source_sense_id": "21726323-26f2-35bd-aee1-7f1a44024f19",
                        "target_lang_word": "besides",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "besides",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ccb3d4bd-f13b-32c2-9fd2-cc72c1126d75",
                                        "entry_id": "5f25d4c4-300f-38fd-9cdb-ad3922a111fd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In addition to."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ff5ad72-d2b5-479a-b283-f54f8a4e9582",
                                                "sense_id": "ccb3d4bd-f13b-32c2-9fd2-cc72c1126d75",
                                                "text": "During the whole time of his abode in the university he generally spent thirteen hours of the day in study; by which assiduity besides an exact dispatch of the whole course of philosophy, he read over in a manner all classic authors that are extant […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "931a6e8b-08f9-3150-b199-0755bc339844",
                                        "entry_id": "5f25d4c4-300f-38fd-9cdb-ad3922a111fd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Other than; except for; instead of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78fac955-d229-4216-bbc4-562286537059",
                                                "sense_id": "931a6e8b-08f9-3150-b199-0755bc339844",
                                                "text": "I don't want to go anywhere besides India."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40ee7dc3-7a61-4041-a403-4442c0a2e5ea",
                                                "sense_id": "931a6e8b-08f9-3150-b199-0755bc339844",
                                                "text": "I want to go with someone besides my father."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68db9b0e-2c56-3426-bcea-870014b198ec",
                                        "entry_id": "5f25d4c4-300f-38fd-9cdb-ad3922a111fd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Beside, next to."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28406662-7eee-4179-8092-718320f40ba5",
                                                "sense_id": "68db9b0e-2c56-3426-bcea-870014b198ec",
                                                "text": "1561, Geneva Bible, Acts 16:13,\nAnd on the Sabbath day, we went out of the citie, beſides a riuer, where they were wont to pray : and we ſate downe, and ſpake vnto the women, which were come together."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1aaa5630-79d0-470d-9704-d095ee7c91f8",
                                                "sense_id": "68db9b0e-2c56-3426-bcea-870014b198ec",
                                                "text": "After this, was Edwin the Kings brother accuſed of ſome conſpiracie by him begun againſt the K. whervpõ he was baniſhed the land, and ſent out in an old rotten veſſell without rower or Marriner, onely accompanied with one Eſquire, ſo that beeing launched foorth from the ſhore, through very diſpaire Edwin lept into the Sea, and drowned himſelfe, but the Eſquire that was with him recouered his body, and broughte it to land at Withſand beſides Canterbury."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9be98b7c-15cb-4da8-966d-62cfb1cf1d34",
                                                "sense_id": "68db9b0e-2c56-3426-bcea-870014b198ec",
                                                "text": "Beſides them both, vpon the ſoiled gras / The dead corſe of an armed knight was ſpred, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "besides",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4408860c-5ab7-3d1f-a27c-1a02973a4ef9",
                                        "entry_id": "af7347af-535a-32d1-b1fb-05abc5d9ffed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Also; in addition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "conjunctive",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6b725c8-3420-4b71-885c-fadd38a6e419",
                                                "sense_id": "4408860c-5ab7-3d1f-a27c-1a02973a4ef9",
                                                "text": "It is besides used as a food, either as a sallad^([sic]), raw, or boiled as greens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2e34614-63de-44df-83e2-0842374a0712",
                                                "sense_id": "4408860c-5ab7-3d1f-a27c-1a02973a4ef9",
                                                "text": "This was but one of Cluny’s hiding-places; he had caves, besides, and underground chambers in several parts of his country; and following the reports of his scouts, he moved from one to another as the soldiers drew near or moved away."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7f5862f-fe22-4475-9d19-8d237b452f49",
                                                "sense_id": "4408860c-5ab7-3d1f-a27c-1a02973a4ef9",
                                                "text": "In the end, Chelsea's organisation and discipline was rewarded but Di Matteo knows they will have to produce the same - and more besides - in the Nou Camp to confirm a meeting with either Real Madrid or Bayern Munich in the final in Munich next month."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57354830-a4c5-31a8-aace-5f2e6050b051",
                                        "entry_id": "af7347af-535a-32d1-b1fb-05abc5d9ffed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to emphasize an additional point, especially an important or stronger reason; moreover; furthermore."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "conjunctive",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73dd7302-85d4-42c2-87de-fbe942836e0f",
                                                "sense_id": "57354830-a4c5-31a8-aace-5f2e6050b051",
                                                "text": "I don't feel like going out tonight. Besides, I have to work tomorrow morning anyway."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "967f728d-0aa9-3baa-a482-aae01f194206",
                                        "entry_id": "af7347af-535a-32d1-b1fb-05abc5d9ffed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Otherwise; else."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92296ee8-672a-439e-b0e0-54b5faebb3fc",
                                                "sense_id": "967f728d-0aa9-3baa-a482-aae01f194206",
                                                "text": "I have been to Spain but nowhere besides."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "904b7255-2e17-305f-bd10-495aa015ad2f",
                                        "entry_id": "af7347af-535a-32d1-b1fb-05abc5d9ffed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "On one side."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f00b59ce-ad11-46de-9ba7-1a9013e73033",
                                                "sense_id": "904b7255-2e17-305f-bd10-495aa015ad2f",
                                                "text": "You are so strongly in my purpose bred\nThat all the world besides methinks are dead"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f40907ce-8590-42d0-9ffc-3716331a5170",
                                                "sense_id": "904b7255-2e17-305f-bd10-495aa015ad2f",
                                                "text": "Yet Teucer would another shaft, at Hectors life dispose;\n So faine, he such a marke would hit: but still besides it goes;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "87585ec8-b7a0-427f-8715-54c526df3e20",
                        "source_entry_id": "bc0c802d-9fd7-3fc1-be25-40c3bf1968b5",
                        "source_sense_id": "21726323-26f2-35bd-aee1-7f1a44024f19",
                        "target_lang_word": "furthermore",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "furthermore",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7526fcbb-63d5-38d5-bec0-ae2a3c124f6e",
                                        "entry_id": "e78316f2-165c-3a6e-af8b-05f5614ea18e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In addition; besides; further; what's more (i.e. to denote additional information)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e86f7438-4301-460f-aca1-180ad4a0a504",
                                                "sense_id": "7526fcbb-63d5-38d5-bec0-ae2a3c124f6e",
                                                "text": "He skillfully took charge of the event, and furthermore, he stayed late after it to clean up."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a647b02-8d83-46cc-b617-c249f76407f2",
                                                "sense_id": "7526fcbb-63d5-38d5-bec0-ae2a3c124f6e",
                                                "text": "He claimed further(more) that he was not even in town the day the murder occured."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "460bd56b-0d5e-4760-91b8-22d4e91ab85d",
                                                "sense_id": "7526fcbb-63d5-38d5-bec0-ae2a3c124f6e",
                                                "text": "But, furthermore, the true Revival of pure Religion, is meeting at this day a still more fearful obstacle, in the system of go-betweenity or theological mermaidism, which has arisen out of the ashes of old defunct infidelity, and is boasting its able champions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebcb7a24-d4a0-4a97-9962-2df41f0bc0f0",
                                                "sense_id": "7526fcbb-63d5-38d5-bec0-ae2a3c124f6e",
                                                "text": "Surprisingly, this analysis revealed that acute exposure to solvent vapors at concentrations below those associated with long-term effects appears to increase the risk of a fatal automobile accident. Furthermore, this increase in risk is comparable to the risk of death from leukemia after long-term exposure to benzene, another solvent, which has the well-known property of causing this type of cancer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
